    ['Which signal carries information in an optical fibre?', 'a light signal', [['a sound signal', 'No. 🔊'], ['a chemical signal', 'No. 🧪'], ['a draught of air', 'No. 🌬️']], 'Light allows very high data rates over long distances.'],
    ['Which kind of wave do wifi and mobile phones use?', 'electromagnetic waves (radio waves)', [['sound waves', 'Sound does not travel to the antenna. 🔊'], ['sea waves', 'No. 🌊'], ['seismic waves', 'Those come from earthquakes. 🌋']], 'They travel even through a vacuum, at the speed of light.'],
    ['What is a digital signal?', 'a signal that only takes two values, coded 0 and 1', [['a signal taking every value', 'That is an analogue signal. 〰️'], ['a signal written in Roman numerals', 'No. 🏛️'], ['a road sign', 'No. 🚦']], 'Computers handle information in digital form.'],
    ['What is the device that receives and decodes a signal called?', 'the receiver', [['the transmitter', 'It sends the signal. 📡'], ['the generator', 'It supplies electrical energy. 🔋'], ['the switch', 'It opens or closes a circuit. 🔘']], 'Example: the phone receives the signal sent by the mast.']
